DOS-PORT (patch 0100, Phase 10 audio offload). Engine-side wiring for
the Phase 10 audio-IRQ instrumentation contract authored by flush-instr
(docs/PHASE10-CONTRACT.md). Pure instrumentation scaffolding — no
backend dispatch logic. Stage 2 MidiScheduler / Stage 3 WaveBlaster /
Stage 4 OPL3 backend implementations land in patches 0101+.

Background: per W20A2 ablation 2026-05-04 (memorialized in
memory/audio_mix_zero_is_not_audio_off.md) and sdl-engine's reanalysis
2026-05-06: the ~13.5 ms / flip audio-IRQ wall-clock cost on g2k
Pentium-OD-83 decomposes into:

  ~1.5 ms music-DMA-mix      (existing g_audio_mix_accum_ns_block bracket)
  ~12.0 ms IRQ-entry/exit     (NEW: irq_wall_us - audio_mix delta)
  variable SFX windows        (NEW: sfx_active_count × per-IRQ cost)

This patch lands the engine-side scaffolding that surfaces these three
slices distinctly, so the W22-WB-A iter can validate Phase 10's
mechanism claim — that the load-bearing lever is DSP idle-pause
removing IRQ-entry/exit overhead, not music-routing alone.

Counter additions per contract § 1 (5 per-block reset + 1 sticky enum):

  uint32_t g_p10_audio_irq_count_block        — IRQ-5 fires within block
  uint32_t g_p10_audio_irq_wall_us_block      — full ISR scope wall-clock
  uint32_t g_p10_audio_idle_pause_count_block — DSP pause→resume transitions
  uint32_t g_p10_audio_idle_pause_us_block    — cumulative paused-µs in block
  uint32_t g_p10_sfx_active_count_block       — IRQs where Pixtone was mixing
  AudioBackend g_p10_audio_backend_active     — sticky; backend selection

Output format per contract § 3.1 — distinct prefix from the existing
`kbd/audio block` and `audio/engine split block` lines:

  [audio-block n=N irq_count=N irq_wall_us=N idle_count=N idle_us=N
   backend=organya|wb|opl3|tracker|none sfx=N]

Two new env vars per contract § 2 (both documented in docs/BOOT.md):

  SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_INSTR=1 (dev-only, strict-1) — gates [audio-block]
    emit. Counter UPDATES are unconditional per anti-pattern #2 so values
    are ready when emit fires. Per-flush cost when env unset: <500 ns.

  SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND={auto,organya,opl3,wb,tracker} (user-
    facing, string-enum) — backend selection. Default `auto` resolves
    to organya in slot 0100 (only backend currently implemented).
    Forced selections (wb / opl3 / tracker) requested-but-unavailable
    fall back to organya gracefully; logged at SoundManager::init.

Cross-vendor lane-split per flush-instr's locked α-API 2026-05-06:

  ENGINE LANE (this patch):
    - Storage decls + definitions (5 numeric + 1 enum)
    - _abl_p10_audio_instr() env helper (cached static-const, strict-1)
    - [audio-block ...] emit + per-block reset in
      _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit() (after wave-23.7 speedup-probe)
    - Engine-side delta-compute pattern: read SDL-side cumulative
      externs (doskutsu_audio_irq_count / _wall_us / _sfx_active_count),
      subtract last-read snapshot, write deltas to per-block storage
    - p10_audio_idle_pause_callback() — registered at SoundManager::
      init() via SDL_DOSAudioRegisterIdlePauseCallback; invoked by SDL
      DSP-pause primitive on each pause→resume transition with
      paused_ns; increments idle_pause_count + accumulates paused_us
    - AudioBackend.{h,cpp} (NEW): selectBackendFromEnv() translates
      SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND env to AudioBackend enum at
      game-init. NO backend dispatch logic; that's Stage 2/3/4.
    - Pixtone.{h,cpp}: g_pixtone_active_count volatile uint32 written
      by Pixtone state machine (++ on play/playResampled success after
      MIX_PlayTrack; -- in pxtSoundDone, balanced via MIX_StopTrack's
      inline callback dispatch on cooperative SDL3-DOS scheduler).
      Read by SDL-side IRQ-5 ISR at handler entry to determine SFX-
      active state (engine-state framing per nx-engine ↔ flush-instr
      ↔ sdl-engine refinement 2026-05-06; semantically correct across
      all three W22-WB-A PLAYs vs ring-observation default).

  SDL LANE (sdl-engine's slots 0037+, NOT in this patch):
    - 3 cross-vendor C-linkage extern variable definitions
      (doskutsu_audio_irq_count / _wall_us / _sfx_active_count)
    - IRQ-5 ISR entry/exit timestamps + cumulative writes
    - DSP idle-pause primitive (pause / resume cycle on idle detect)
    - SDL_DOSAudioRegisterIdlePauseCallback API + force-pause/resume
      diagnostic helpers
    - IRQ handler increments doskutsu_audio_sfx_active_count when
      g_pixtone_active_count > 0 at entry (engine-state framing)

Standalone build of this patch fails at link with 4 expected unresolved
references — `doskutsu_audio_irq_count`, `doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us`,
`doskutsu_audio_sfx_active_count`, `SDL_DOSAudioRegisterIdlePauseCallback`.
This is the W22A combined-review precedent: both lanes' diffs land
together, build-qa runs the combined smoke. Compile is clean (no
warnings); linker errors resolve when sdl-engine's slots 0037+ land
alongside.

