+// DOS-PORT (patch 0100, Phase 10 audio offload — instrumentation
+// scaffolding): gate the [audio-block ...] emit on the env var per
+// docs/PHASE10-CONTRACT.md § 2.1. Strict-"1" match; default OFF
+// (instrumentation has its own per-flush cost — 3 SDL-side cumulative
+// reads + delta-compute + 1 LOG_INFO emission per 100-flip block).
+// Cached static-const-bool — -O2 hoists per-flush guards. Pairs with
+// SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND (user-facing backend selector) per
+// the design's two-hint pattern: AUDIO_INSTR is dev-only diagnostic
+// emission; AUDIO_BACKEND is the runtime backend choice (independent
+// from instrumentation).
+//
+// Per contract § 2.1 anti-pattern #2: this gate controls EMIT only,
+// NOT counter UPDATES. Counters increment unconditionally so values
+// are ready when emit fires; engine-side delta-compute reads SDL-side
+// cumulative externs unconditionally so the prior-snapshot read at
+// each [audio-block] flush stays accurate. Per-flush cost when env
+// unset: ~3 atomic reads + 5 subtractions + 5 stores; <500 ns.
+inline bool _abl_p10_audio_instr()
+{
+  static const bool v = _strict_truthy_env("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_INSTR");
+  return v;
+}
